   "text": {
    "L1": "Two figures are congruent when one can be placed exactly over the other.",
    "L2": "They must have the same shape and the same size. We test this by superposition.",
    "L3": "Here is a common myth: matching shape alone is enough, whatever the size.",
    "L4": "That is not true. A smaller copy with the same shape cannot cover a larger one exactly.",
    "L5": "Trace the first figure, then place the tracing on the second figure.",
    "L6": "You may slide, turn or flip the tracing. These movements do not change congruence.",
    "L7": "If every side and every corner lines up, the figures are congruent; matching parts are equal.",
    "L8": "Now choose the test that decides whether two figures are congruent."
   },
